{
  "about": [
    "Shared cases for decoding a candidate identity into the pick-board row_key. Both sides read this file:",
    "customizations/pick-workbench/tests/mirror/test_mirror_identity_cases.py checks row_key (gates.row_key_of) and identity (DramaInput.identity);",
    "frontend/tests/unit/core/pick/identity.test.ts checks rowKeyFromSourceId against row_key and rowKeyFromIdentity against card_row_key.",
    "identity is json.dumps([source, source_id, language], ensure_ascii=False, separators=(',', ':')) (ggwork_pick/contracts.py); source_id is",
    "Buffer.from(rowKey).toString('base64url') (realshort@816ca2e src/lib/pick/feed-map.ts:316): base64url, no padding.",
    "row_key: base64url alphabet only, decodes, strict UTF-8 (a leading BOM is kept), and re-encoding gives source_id back; else null.",
    "card_row_key: row_key when it also passes isRowKey (non-empty, <= 120 UTF-16 units, not all whitespace, no C0 control or DEL), else null.",
    "Expected values are written by design (the key that was encoded, or null), not by running either decoder."
  ],
